          },
          {
            "value": "Live",
            "label": "This site, on a 1GB server"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-figure",
      "data": {
        "caption_left": "Fig. 01 · the cg-cms admin, chrisgarlick.com",
        "caption_right": "A cached page: 0.4 ms, live 1GB server",
        "tone": "plain",
        "image": {
          "file": "media/cg-cms-admin-dashboard.png",
          "alt": "The cg-cms admin dashboard at chrisgarlick.com: alerts, published and draft counts, leads this week, page cache warmth and recent articles"
        },
        "frame": "browser",
        "frame_url": "chrisgarlick.com"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "01\nTHE *problem*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "I wanted a CMS I could edit comfortably, that stayed fast on a small server, without paying for a platform or fighting a page builder. Nothing off the shelf did all three, so I built it.",
        "background": "tinted"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "02\nHOW IT *works*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Content lives in Postgres and is edited in an Inertia and React admin built from typed blocks, so content can't break the layout. When a page is saved, cg-cms renders it once and writes the HTML to disk. Visitors are served that file, without PHP or the database.",
        "background": "tinted"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-stats",
      "data": {
        "tone": "tinted",
        "stats": [
          {
            "value": "0.4 ms",
            "label": "To serve a cached page, live 1GB server"
          },
          {
            "value": "6,300",
            "label": "Requests a second on a 1GB, single-CPU server"
          },
          {
            "value": "26 to 29 ms",
            "label": "Cold render, measured on my laptop"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-split",
      "data": {
        "eyebrow": "03 · The hard part",
        "title": "THE FAST PATH *skips Laravel.*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "Laravel itself costs about 13.6 ms before any of my code runs, so no amount of tuning inside the app would get close to a static file. Saving a page renders it once and writes it to disk; a visitor never touches PHP or Postgres. Measured on the live 1GB server, from the server itself: time to first byte with curl, best of 20 requests with the connection setup taken off, and throughput with ab and keep-alive, 5,000 requests at 20 at a time.",
        "media": "card",
        "card_label": "Time to first byte · cg-cms, live 1GB server",
        "card_title": "0.4 ms a page\n6,300 a second",
        "background": "plain",
        "panel": "none",
        "swap": false
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "kit-text-block",
      "data": {
        "title": "04\nFOR *clients*",
        "heading_level": "2",
        "body": "The same approach works for any Laravel site that's mostly read: content you can edit yourself, pages that load at once, and a small server bill.",
        "background": "tinted",
        "link_label": "Start a Laravel project",
        "link_url": "/start"
      }
    },
